From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:57:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] include: all of Windows.UI.Composition, as Windows' metadata
 declares it, and its interop.

Office's AirSpace uses 64 interfaces of Windows.UI.Composition and its Core,
Interactions and Diagnostics namespaces; the IDL here had 33 of them.  The file is
now written from Windows.UI.winmd by scripts/winmd-idl.py: every type of the five
namespaces, with its IID, contract and vtable order, the parameterized interfaces
they use declared.  Windows.Graphics.DirectX gains the two enums it refers to,
DirectXColorSpace and DirectXPrimitiveTopology.

The interop interfaces come from the SDK's header rather than the metadata:
ICompositorDesktopInterop, the drawing surface and graphics device interop,
ICompositionCapabilitiesInteropFactory, IVisualInteractionSourceInterop and
IDesktopWindowTargetInterop, each IID checked against Windows' dcomp.dll.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b26744bba07bf33eab043f46a9463833d8ef1936)

